   $q$A random sample of 50 students at a school of 1,000 found these favorite sports: Soccer: 18, Basketball: 15, Swimming: 10, Other: 7. About how many more students at the school prefer soccer than prefer swimming?$q$, $q$[{"text":"200","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-one-group-only"},{"text":"160","is_correct":true},{"text":"8","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-scale-to-population"},{"text":"360","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"scaled-only-one-group"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$160$q$, $q$Soccer is estimated at $18 \times 20 = 360$ students and swimming at $10 \times 20 = 200$, so the difference is $360 - 200 = 160$. The choice 8 is the difference in the sample, which still has to be scaled up to the whole school.$q$, 'draft', null)
