   $q$Four students each took a random sample of 20 students from their school of 700 and counted how many bring lunch from home. Their counts were: 6, 8, 7, 7. Using all four samples, what is the best estimate of the number of students at the school who bring lunch from home?$q$, $q$[{"text":"980","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-divide-by-number-of-samples"},{"text":"210","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-only-one-sample"},{"text":"28","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-scale-to-population"},{"text":"245","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$245$q$, $q$Together the samples have $6 + 8 + 7 + 7 = 28$ lunch bringers out of 80 students, or $\frac{28}{80} = 0.35$, and $0.35 \times 700 = 245$. The choice 210 uses only the first sample of 6 out of 20.$q$, 'draft', null)
