   $q$A random sample of 50 students at a school of 900 found that 18 want a longer lunch period. A second random sample of 50 students found that 22 want a longer lunch period. What is the most reasonable range for the number of students at the school who want a longer lunch period?$q$, $q$[{"text":"From 18 to 22 students","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-scale-to-population"},{"text":"From about 324 to about 396 students","is_correct":true},{"text":"Exactly 360 students and no other number","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thinks-sample-is-exact"},{"text":"From about 504 to about 576 students","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-the-wrong-part"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$From about 324 to about 396 students$q$, $q$The samples suggest rates of $\frac{18}{50} = 0.36$ and $\frac{22}{50} = 0.44$, which give $0.36 \times 900 = 324$ and $0.44 \times 900 = 396$. The choice 504 to 576 estimates the students who do not want a longer lunch.$q$, 'draft', null)
