  ('1965a83a-0739-5d24-aa0c-9ce6820109ae', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'math-g7-sampling-and-inference'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Rosa surveyed a random sample of 25 students and found that 40 percent want a school garden. Theo surveyed a random sample of 200 students at the same school and found that 46 percent want a garden. Whose estimate is probably more reliable, and why?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Theo's, because Theo's random sample is much larger","is_correct":true},{"text":"They are equally reliable because both samples are random","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-sample-size"},{"text":"Rosa's, because Rosa's percent is lower","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"judged-by-the-result"},{"text":"Rosa's, because a smaller sample has fewer mistakes","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thinks-smaller-is-better"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Theo's, because Theo's random sample is much larger$q$, $q$Both samples are random, but a larger random sample usually gives an estimate closer to the true value, so Theo's 200 students is more reliable. Being random removes bias, but a small sample of 25 can still vary a lot by chance.$q$, 'draft', null)
