   $q$A random sample of 40 students at a school of 1,200 were asked how they get to school: Bus: 22, Car: 10, Walk: 6, Bike: 2. The principal says, "More than half of our students ride the bus." Is this claim supported, and about how many bus riders are there?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Yes, about 880 students ride the bus","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"scaled-by-wrong-factor"},{"text":"Yes, about 660 students ride the bus","is_correct":true},{"text":"No, only 22 students ride the bus","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-sample-count-as-population-count"},{"text":"No, about 540 students ride the bus","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-the-wrong-part"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Yes, about 660 students ride the bus$q$, $q$Bus riders are $\frac{22}{40} = 0.55$ of the sample, so about $0.55 \times 1200 = 660$ students ride the bus, which is more than half of 1,200. The answer about 540 students counts everyone who does not ride the bus.$q$, 'draft', null)
